This skill combines and modifies four upstream projects.

  Japanese patterns derive from https://github.com/iKora128/stop-ai-slop-jp
  English patterns derive from https://github.com/hardikpandya/stop-slop
  Japanese comma, vocabulary, and syntax rules partly derive from
    https://github.com/AnIT012/nihongo
    https://github.com/nanaism/yomiyasu

Their patterns are spread across policies/ and scripts/. SKILL.md, README.md,
and the split into per-policy files are original to this repository. All four
upstreams are MIT licensed; their notices follow.

The Japanese pattern classification and examples trace back to the note article
"その文章、AIに書かせただろ" by だいち (GENSHI AI):
https://note.com/ikora/n/n0bbb2828b91e

